      "message": "semantics were copied (the contract I read had version 2, so v2 behavior is implemented: concatenation of `id` and `attempt` with `':'`, defaulting `attempt` to the string `'0'`).\n- `idempotency_key(request)` reimplements the contract logic directly (`request['id'] + ':' + request.get('attempt', '0')`) \u2014 no import of, or runtime call into, `semkg_contract`.\n- A `__main__` block that asserts the two behaviors.\n\n**Verification (small local check, not repository-wide)**\n- Imported `producer` from the attempt dir and asserted `CONTRACT_VERSION == 2`, `idempotency_key({'id':'A','attempt':'2'}) == 'A:2'`, and `idempotency_key({'id':'A'}) == 'A:0'` \u2014 all passed (exit code 0, no assertion errors).\n- Note: a `cd \u2026 && python producer.py` form was rejected by the tool (only bare python commands allowed), so I used `python -c` with `sys.path` insertion instead; the module-level asserts therefore ran under import of the equivalent logic, not via `__main__`.\n\nNo other files were created or modified."
